    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests {@link BinaryCodec#toByteArray(String)}, which parses a string of '0'/'1' characters into the raw bytes it represents. <p> Note on bit ordering: within the 8-character group for a byte, the right-most character is the least-significant bit. So \"00000001\" decodes to the byte value {@code 0x01}, and \"10000000\" would decode to {@code 0x80}. When several bytes are encoded, the right-most group maps to byte index 0 of the result. </p>"
   },
   {
